{"seq":49,"slug":"database-design-modeling","title":"数据库设计与建模","stage":"DONE","category":"cs-fundamentals","chapterCount":4,"docCount":12,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/database-design-modeling","rating":{"composite":3.61,"verdict":"stable","groups":{"quality":3.8,"coverage":3,"positioning":null,"strategic":4},"weights":{"quality":0.3,"coverage":0.25,"positioning":0.2,"strategic":0.25},"profile":null},"introMarkdown":"# 数据库设计与建模\n\n把现实世界的事实搬进数据库，从来不是「画几张表」那么简单。一个订单系统里，「顾客」「商品」「订单」之间的关系怎么落到表结构上，键怎么设，冗余该不该留，分析报表又该走另一套什么模型——这些决定一旦写进生产库，往往要陪伴系统数年，改动成本极高。数据建模就是在写下第一条 `CREATE TABLE` 之前，把这些决定想清楚的学科。\n\n本 hub 用四章把这门学科从地基铺到当下实践，四条主线层层递进，后一章都建立在前一章的概念之上。\n\n第一章「基础」回答最根本的问题：建模到底在建什么。它区分概念、逻辑、物理三个抽象层级，讲实体关系（ER）建模如何把业务语言翻译成结构化的实体与联系，再讲关系模型如何用「关系」「键」「完整性约束」这套严谨的数学语言承接 ER 图。这一章定下整个 hub 的词汇表。\n\n第二章「规范化」处理「同一份事实不要存两遍」这个核心矛盾。它从函数依赖这一形式化工具讲起——这是判断「冗余」的数学依据——再用一系列范式（1NF 到 BCNF 乃至 4NF）给出消除冗余的递进标准，最后承认现实并不总是越规范越好，转入反规范化的权衡：为了读性能，何时该主动把拆开的表合回去。\n\n第三章「分析型建模」转向另一个世界。前两章服务于事务处理（OLTP），追求写入正确与少冗余；而面向分析（OLAP）的数仓恰恰反其道而行。这一章讲维度建模与星型模式如何为「快速聚合查询」优化，讲数仓的各类模式（雪花、星座、数据金库、宽表）如何取舍，并专门拆解缓慢变化维这个分析建模里最易出错的细节。\n\n第四章「现代实践」把视野拉到当下。当数据不再只装进一种关系库，NoSQL 的文档、键值、宽列、图模型各有各的建模范式（以「访问模式优先」为纲）；模式不再一次定死，而要随业务持续演进与迁移；不同负载用不同存储，多模存储与选型成了架构师的日常决策。\n\n四章读完，你会有一条完整的心智链：从「怎么把世界想清楚」（基础），到「怎么把它存得干净」（规范化），到「怎么把它查得飞快」（分析型建模），再到「在多样化的今天怎么选对工具」（现代实践）。建议顺序阅读；每篇都会在引用其它篇主讲的概念时给出交叉链接，方便随时回溯。\n","chapters":[{"seq":1,"slug":"foundations","title":"基础","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/database-design-modeling/foundations","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"data-modeling-overview","title":"数据建模总览","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/database-design-modeling/foundations/data-modeling-overview"},{"seq":2,"slug":"er-modeling","title":"实体关系建模","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/database-design-modeling/foundations/er-modeling"},{"seq":3,"slug":"relational-model","title":"关系模型与键","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/database-design-modeling/foundations/relational-model"}]},{"seq":2,"slug":"normalization","title":"规范化","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/database-design-modeling/normalization","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"functional-dependencies","title":"函数依赖","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/database-design-modeling/normalization/functional-dependencies"},{"seq":2,"slug":"normal-forms","title":"范式","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/database-design-modeling/normalization/normal-forms"},{"seq":3,"slug":"denormalization","title":"反规范化权衡","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/database-design-modeling/normalization/denormalization"}]},{"seq":3,"slug":"analytical-modeling","title":"分析型建模","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/database-design-modeling/analytical-modeling","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"dimensional-modeling","title":"维度建模与星型","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/database-design-modeling/analytical-modeling/dimensional-modeling"},{"seq":2,"slug":"data-warehouse-schemas","title":"数仓模式","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/database-design-modeling/analytical-modeling/data-warehouse-schemas"},{"seq":3,"slug":"slowly-changing-dimensions","title":"缓慢变化维","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/database-design-modeling/analytical-modeling/slowly-changing-dimensions"}]},{"seq":4,"slug":"modern","title":"现代实践","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/database-design-modeling/modern","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"nosql-data-modeling","title":"NoSQL 数据建模","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/database-design-modeling/modern/nosql-data-modeling"},{"seq":2,"slug":"schema-evolution-migration","title":"模式演进与迁移","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/database-design-modeling/modern/schema-evolution-migration"},{"seq":3,"slug":"polyglot-persistence","title":"多模存储与选型","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/database-design-modeling/modern/polyglot-persistence"}]}]}